    "field": "Climate-wildfire interactions",
    "problem": "The compound nature of wildfires and complex physical processes make it difficult to directly connect wildfire changes in the western U.S. with specific drivers of anthropogenic climate change, such as diminishing Arctic sea ice.",
    "method": "This study uses observations, reanalysis data, climate model sensitivity experiments, and a multi-model ensemble of climate simulations to demonstrate and explain the teleconnection between declining Arctic sea ice and increasing fire-favorable weather that fuels large wildfires over the western United States.",
    "task": "The task is to demonstrate and explain the link between diminishing Arctic sea ice and increasing large wildfires in the western United States using observations, climate model sensitivity experiments, and multi-model climate simulations to analyze the resulting atmospheric teleconnections and fire-favorable weather.",
